{"authored" [{"question" "q-51251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The population of pines in a forest increases by $100$ trees every year. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the population $P(t)$ of the pines? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in years." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the pines population is $P,$ then the rate of change of the population is $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in years.\n\nSince $100$ new pines are added every year, the rate of change of the population of the pines is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=100.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The number of completed online course enrollments increases by $18$ enrollments every hour during a promotional event. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of enrollments $E(t)?$ Assume that the time $t$ is measured in hours.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the number of enrollments is $E,$ then the rate of change of the number of enrollments is $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in hours.\n\nSince $18$ new enrollments are added every hour, the rate of change of the number of enrollments is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=18.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The number of bacteria in a particular crop at any given moment decreases at a rate that is proportional to the number of bacteria at that moment.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of bacteria $B$ at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of bacteria** in a particular crop at any given moment **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to **the number of bacteria** at that moment..* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of bacteria* in a particular crop varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of bacteria* at the moment. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}∝B.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of bacteria *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{B},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-kB,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=B"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{B},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-51254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k-\\frac{1}{B},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Some people in a community contracted an unknown virus. The number of people infected by the virus increases at a rate that is proportional to the number of people infected by the virus. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of people who contracted the virus, $V,$ at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of people** infected by the virus **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **number of people** infected by the virus.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of people* infected by the virus varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of people* infected. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝V.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of people infected by the virus  *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k+V,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k-V,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=tV"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=V"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "When heated, the concentration $C(t)$ of oxygen in water decreases at a rate that's proportional to the concentration of oxygen in the water at that moment. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the oxygen concentration at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*When heated, the **concentration** $C(t)$ of oxygen in water **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **concentration** of oxygen in the water at that moment.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *concentration* of oxygen in water varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *concentration* of oxygen in the water. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}∝C.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the concentration of oxygen *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-kC.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\