fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{S}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The volume of water $V$ in a pool being filled increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the square of the volume of water in the pool at that moment. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of water $V$ in the pool?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The  **volume of water** $V$  in a pool being filled **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the ** square of the volume of water** $V$ in the pool at that moment. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume of water* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the volume.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume of water *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refer