}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the value *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041831/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c53d0ee6a7501c92f48514b41a995b101200d5c0210307e8a46b6dcc30363fc"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5352fdf86e6abe82c17a6566dd848951ebe0972ce1864ab53dbaae9fcdf8bb84"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041831/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c53d0ee6a7501c92f48514b41a995b101200d5c0210307e8a46b6dcc30363fc"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kV,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{V},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041831/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c53d0ee6a7501c92f48514b41a995b101200d5c0210307e8a46b6dcc30363fc"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/corr