*rate* at which the *number of sales* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of sales squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}∝{S}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of sales *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k{S}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041831/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c53d0ee6a7501c92f48514b41a995b101200d5c0210307e8a46b6dcc30363fc"} {"question" "q-143031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041831/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5352fdf86e6abe82c17a6566dd848951ebe0972ce1864ab53dbaae9fcdf8bb84"} {"question" "q-143031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041831/state.json" "file_sha256" "6c53d0ee6a7501c92f48514b41a995b101200d5c0210307e8a46b6dcc30363fc"} {"question" "q-143031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{S},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k{S}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{S}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{S},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=k{S}^{2},\\,\\,k>0